Goal: connect the modules of the design already in the problem state into one buildable plant file, and store it with build_plant as design/base.

Read first: the problem state's `design` (its `modules` list with ids and types, its `owners`, its `choices.cooling_route` with the two groups absorption/compression, and `size.doublets` {min 1, max 3}); then `read_case` (all sections) for the site, demand temperatures and requirements; `describe_module` for every module type you connect (ports, inlets, outlets, parameters).

What to hand back: the plant file (format 1, kind plant, a name) with
- `modules`: exactly the state's modules, keyed by their ids, each with its `type`;
- `connections`: every port of every module connected or named as a plant inlet/outlet, physically sensible: d0 (Doublet) production -> filters -> degasser -> heat_exchanger brine side -> injection_pump -> d0 injection; heat_exchanger secondary -> heating_supply_pipe -> heating_consumer -> heating_return_pipe -> back to the exchanger; peak_boiler in parallel on the heating supply; cooling_consumer loop through cooling_supply_pipe/cooling_return_pipe with the compression route (compression_chiller + compression_cooler) and the absorption route (drive_splitter -> absorption_chiller -> drive_mixer, absorption_cooler) as the two `choices.cooling_route` groups; electricity_grid feeding the ESP, injection pump, boiler, chillers and coolers; flare fed by the degasser gas and venting to atmosphere; coolers rejecting to atmosphere;
